1. Verification via curl Pipeline
Run a sequential loop from your local terminal to confirm that incoming requests alternate between backend nodes in a Round-Robin pattern:

for i in {1..4}; do curl -s http://<YOUR_EC2_PUBLIC_IP> | grep "Instance"; done


Expected Output:

<h1>🟢 Backend App Instance 1</h1>
      <h1>🟣 Backend App Instance 2</h1>
      <h1>🟢 Backend App Instance 1</h1>
      <h1>🟣 Backend App Instance 2</h1>

2. Failover Resilience Test
Simulate an outage by stopping app-1:

pm2 stop app-1

Re-run the curl test sweep. Nginx will detect the failed node and automatically pass 100% of live traffic to app-2 without returning 502 Bad Gateway errors to the client!

